            <ArticleTitle>Hepatic subcapsular hematoma: a rare late complication after ERCP.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>234-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a clinical case of a 83 years old man, who consulted to the Emergency Department by continuous pain in right upper quadrant, having been discharged a week ago after ERCP for choledocholithiasis. TAC was performed showing a subcapsular hematoma without active bleeding. This complication post ERCP has been described on few occasions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
